%% section: Consistency, repair, tombstones
%% caption: Tombstones and why deletes hurt reads
flowchart TB
    DEL["DELETE a row"] --> TS["Writes a tombstone — a marker, not a removal"]
    TS --> WHY["Needed so a replica that was down does not resurrect the row"]
    TS --> READ["Reads must scan past every tombstone in range"]
    READ --> SLOW["A partition full of tombstones reads slowly, then fails on the threshold"]
    TS --> GC["gc_grace_seconds — kept this long before compaction can drop it"]
    GC --> REPAIR{"Repair run within that window?"}
    REPAIR -->|"No"| ZOMBIE["Deleted data can come back"]
    REPAIR -->|"Yes"| SAFE["Tombstone compacted away safely"]
    ANTI["Anti-pattern: queue-like tables with constant deletes"] -.-> SLOW
